ravity pulls you back down. Scales measure weight from gravity’s pull.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the observations, properties or test steps used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Gravity idea.","caption":"Acts on all objects.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Gravity</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">pull toward Earth</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Effect</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">things fall / weight</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Everyday gravity evidence.","caption":"Write your definition.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Drop</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">ball and scarf</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Both</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">fall downward</text></g></svg>"}],"year_level":"Year 3"}') WHERE seed_key='s2-sci-y3-w18-l1' AND family_id IS NULL;
